# Derived by hand from Appendix B (`!Except` fires the left event in a tick in which the right does not fire) and Type System ch. 4 (the call in the plain function is not lifted; `10 +` is lifted over its firing): in the first tick both fire and nothing is heard; in the second the left fires alone, 10 + 1. Never run.
test t

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="left")
    1: Ui.Button(label="right")
    2: Ui.Label(text="0: 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
    1: click

tick 2
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="1: 11")
